{
  "text": " When does America wake up? I mean, what is it gonna take? Because the doctors are seeing these deaths that are happening to young kids, and they're basically, they're like, look in the other way, they're saying, hey, I'm not gonna jeopardize my job, another kid, another vaccine, and they're shutting up about it, right? And there's nothing breaking that cycle here because they don't wanna lose their job. So how do we break this thing open? I mean, it's the biggest thing, the best historical parallel I can draw is Chernobyl. So after Chernobyl, the Soviet Union decided to convince everybody that there'd been no medical fallout from all that radioactivity. And when people came forward with clear problems, doctors were told to tell them they have phobia, they have radiophobia, and they tried to make that last, and it lasted actually for two years. But then there was just so much blowback because so many injuries, and when you had kids being born, babies being born with fishtails, you had calves with, their leg was next to their ear, you could only get away with that for so long. And even the Soviet Union and its totalitarian system arguably collapsed over the lives of Chernobyl. And I think the lies that have been spun out in defense of this mass medical experimentation of horrific failure, I think as the injuries accumulate and people start asking the right questions, and people start making the right inquiries, and enough conscientious doctors and nurses continue to come forward, it will at some point reach a critical mass that the system collapses. And I think the system will regret it because it will lead to people never trusting them for generations because of what they've done.",
